# KiwiClaw PCM session per-clip stereo balance implementation report

Date: 2026-08-29

## Product outcome

KiwiClaw can now set an independent stereo balance on every saved PCM clip. Each stereo clip exposes `片段声像` with the closed choices left 100%, left 50%, center, right 50%, and right 100%. The setting drives single-clip export, combined local preview, and combined WAV download.

Moving left preserves the left sample and attenuates only the right sample; moving right preserves the right sample and attenuates only the left sample. Mono clips remain centered and cannot acquire a non-zero balance. Changing balance immediately pauses and revokes any prepared combined preview. `播放原片段` continues to audition the original source range without this derived session transform.

## Construction choice

A parallel UI balance array and a temporary Web Audio panner were rejected because they would let preview state drift from saved clip order and exported bytes. `balancePermille` instead lives in the existing exact session-range selection, is restored through its closed-shape verifier, and is applied by the one deterministic session-WAV builder.

