## Outcome

After the browser has decoded the explicitly selected local original image and its intrinsic geometry still matches the verified source geometry, the user can now rotate that current local view by an exact right angle and explicitly save the result as a PNG.

The exported pixels use the original source dimensions rather than the current display zoom. This makes the existing local rotation view produce a reusable user-owned artifact without adding a Rust/Tauri command, backend image pipeline, automatic filesystem write, or new authority.

